# Runs B and C, same evening, same window and shape. The nvme module was reloaded with
# poll_queues=1 first, and /sys/block/nvme0n1/queue/io_poll printed 1.
# Photographs: linux-fio-pvsync2-{read,write}.jpg and linux-fio-io_uring-{write,read}.jpg, at https://github.com/nifeos/nife/tree/cd8fefa3c68fd170e9e92f2747276ab47e9ddacf/bench/xenon-2026-10-04

# Run B (bench clock about 23:20): --ioengine=pvsync2 --hipri, read then write.
# Polling did NOT engage: ctx=16384 on read, 16385 on write (one switch per I/O).
B read:   IOPS=30.5k, BW=126MB/s, 64.0MiB in 533 ms
          clat (usec): avg=31.87, median=27, p99=87, p99.99=12518
B write:  IOPS=66.3k, BW=272MB/s, 64.0MiB in 247 ms
          clat (usec): avg=14.40, median=13, p99=28, p99.99=2737

# Run C (bench clock about 23:25): --ioengine=io_uring --hipri, write FIRST then read
# (nife's order). Polling engaged: ctx=12 on write, ctx=4 on read; sys 84% and 95%.
C write:  IOPS=104k, BW=425MB/s, 64.0MiB in 158 ms
